{"type":"text","timestamp":1794545871422,"sessionID":"ses_e2cbe0a45ffeC9C8e26lVMH2DA","part":{"id":"prt_1d344dad2001icNHxs1j6cn7sT","sessionID":"ses_e2cbe0a45ffeC9C8e26lVMH2DA","messageID":"msg_1d344caad001MfgJkikAfTMtF2","type":"text","text":"T003 is complete.\n\n## Files written\n\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/claude.mjs`\n  - Added `injectedFromEntries(entries)` plus a private `attachmentText(content)` helper. It collects every `attachment` / `hook_additional_context` entry, stringifies its `content` (string as-is, array by joining string items and each item's `text` with `\\n`), and returns `[{ source: 'hook_additional_context', text }]` for each non-empty text in file order.\n  - Added `injected: injectedFromEntries(entries)` to the ok result of `loadClaudeSession`, immediately after `records`. Nothing else changed.\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/claude.test.mjs`\n  - Added one case: a Claude fixture with the `hook_additional_context` attachment line loads with `injected` equal to `[{ source: 'hook_additional_context', text: BRIEF }]` and the same `records` length as the same fixture without the attachment.\n\n## Verify output\n\nCommand: `node --test .skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/claude.test.mjs`\n\n```\n✔ a parent transcript resolves by its recorded session id (2.323ms)\n✔ a user message that carries text and a tool result keeps both entries (1.300125ms)\n✔ a transcript outside the store is refused without reading it (2.005416ms)\n✔ a subagent transcript is refused as the parent session (1.188167ms)\n✔ a transcript that declares another session is a session_mismatch (1.498ms)\n✔ a missing transcript_path is a locator_unavailable (0.074291ms)\n✔ an absent transcript is an error when the store is present (1.150917ms)\n✔ an unreadable store is reported without throwing (0.39875ms)\n✔ a local command report stays out of the history and the typed command stays in (1.218625ms)\n✔ a hook additional context attachment is returned as injected text (2.419375ms)\nℹ tests 10\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 10\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 69.1445\nexit=0\n```\n\n(`fail 0`, exit 0.) The diff covers only the two files T003 names, and I did not tick the checkbox in `tasks.md`.\n\n## Not done\n\nNothing. The whole-reader suite (`VSR`) was not run because other workers are editing `pi.mjs`, `devin.mjs` and `dsh.mjs` concurrently and T003's verify names only the Claude test file.","time":{"start":1794545867474,"end":1794545871422}}}
